  "notes": ["Each plane is an unedited normal Sasuke role-20 descriptor bound by original code to a declared owner and rigid matrix. The two foreign planes have separate active seats; the same-owner control publishes but is not a foreign candidate.","The near plane reaches the original narrow and support path, producing the captured negative Y vector and root Y 124. The far plane fails the original broad helper when replayed from its exact captured scratch operands.","A far test after near support refreshes the reference with the adjusted role-10 sphere bottom before broad rejection. A far test before support, or no second plane, leaves the earlier value unchanged. The far test is not a support contact.","The following wall pass compares the published role-08 bottom against that reference, admitting equality. Only the tested order with a refresh and an admitted sphere produces +20 X.","Both an isolated pass sequence and the original enclosing walk produce the same state through the presentation frontier. This does not establish retail prop construction, animated platform support, live arena behavior or native gameplay."],
